infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title koffi vs ffi-napi: the choice is not close in 2025
  desc Both call a prebuilt .so, but only one escapes the compiler FFI was meant to avoid
  compares
    - label koffi — the senior default
      children
        - label Prebuilt binaries
          desc Ships per-platform binaries — no node-gyp, no compiler at install
        - label Actively maintained
          desc Tracks Node ABI changes; install survives a Node major upgrade
        - label Measurably faster calls
          desc Lower per-call marshalling overhead than the legacy stack
        - label First-class struct & pointer types
          desc Structs, pointers, output params, callbacks, disposables built in
    - label ffi-napi + ref-napi — legacy
      children
        - label Itself a native addon
          desc Installing compiles C — the whole node-gyp / prebuild / ABI matrix
        - label Breaks on Node majors
          desc Every ABI shift rebuilds ref-napi; pin Node or npm install dies
        - label Effectively unmaintained
          desc No active upkeep — do not start new work on it
        - label Migrate off it
          desc Treat as legacy you port to koffi, not a starting point
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
